{"availability":"available","full":"lourd/react-router-transitions","name":"react-router-transitions","description":"Small demo of how to animate transitions between routes with React Router v4","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":10,"forks":0,"created":"2017-06-08T21:03:05Z","updated":"2022-12-07T01:25:45Z","branch":"master","homepage":"https://lourd.github.io/react-router-transitions/","topics":["animations","demo","react","react-router","routing","transitions"],"demo":"https://reacttraining.com/react-router/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T01:25:47.231Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T01:25:47.231Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T01:25:47.231Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T01:25:47.231Z","stars":10,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This is a small toy app demonstrating how to animate transitioning between routes with React Router (v4+).","Understanding the nuance of animating route transitions when using an array of route objects, the Switch component, and positioning the pages is very tricky. I was motivated to make this after misunderstanding it myself several times during projects, and after observing all of the confusion in react-router#4351.","By using the withRouter decorator/function/higher-order component, the App component receives the location as a prop. That's then passed down a prop to the Switch component, which in turn passes it down to each of the child Routes to use for computing whether it's matched or not. Passing location as a prop to Switch or Route overrides their default behavior of getting the location from context. We need to do this so that the exiting Switch and Route components keep the \"old\" location, instead of getting the new one."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lourd/react-router-transitions/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"6b0e2e111f77d27b5af915660e14a1442b1c273b3736d2d8610cbbb8227f8d7b","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T01:25:47.363Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T01:25:47.363Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This is a small toy app demonstrating how to animate transitioning between routes with React Router (v4+).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lourd/react-router-transitions/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"6b0e2e111f77d27b5af915660e14a1442b1c273b3736d2d8610cbbb8227f8d7b","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lourd/react-router-transitions/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T01:25:47.363Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2022-12-07T01:25:45Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lourd/react-router-transitions/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T01:25:47.363Z","hash":"6b0e2e111f77d27b5af915660e14a1442b1c273b3736d2d8610cbbb8227f8d7b","originalBytes":2354,"storedBytes":2354,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["switch","location","route","component","new","using","when","app","getting","instead","key","old","same","which","after","because","before","components","decorator","don","down","git","history","how","install","keep","location.key","need","npm","one","prop","react","router","routes","transitions","why","withrouter","animate","animating","app.js","array","behavior","between","child","clicking","clone","code","computing","confusion","context","copies","default","demo","demonstrating","did","different","does","during","each","element.","exit","exiting","faq","first","function","generates","get","going","guarantees","happens","higher-order","link","location.pathname","make","matched","meat","misunderstanding","motivated","myself","node.js","not.","nuance","objects","observing","occurs.","one.","out","overrides","page","pages","passed","passes","passing","path","path.","pathname","positioning","projects","prop.","react-router-transitions","react-router#4351","receives","render","rendered","renders","see","several","small","src","start","their","there","times","toy","tra